This paper takes that contradiction as its subject. Our approach is a
subtraction with a matched control. Writing $h_{\text{no}}$, $h_{\text{wrong}}$
and $h_{\text{skill}}$ for the residual state at the last prompt position under
no document, a length-matched wrong skill, and the gold skill,
\begin{equation}
\underbrace{h_{\text{skill}} - h_{\text{no}}}_{\tvec\ \text{(total)}}
\;=\;
\underbrace{h_{\text{wrong}} - h_{\text{no}}}_{\gvec\ \text{(presence)}}
\;+\;
\underbrace{h_{\text{skill}} - h_{\text{wrong}}}_{\dvec\ \text{(content)}} ,
\label{eq:decomp}
\end{equation}
an identity, not an approximation. The question is which side of it does the
work. We answer it by adding each component back to the no-document state and
measuring what the model then does.

\paragraph{What the decomposition is a decomposition of.} One result shapes how
everything below should be read, so we state it first. A patch applied anywhere
\emph{other than the document's own tokens} transports the model's
\emph{decision}, not the document's content. On third-party clinical skills,
transplanting the document's own several-hundred token states reproduces its
entire effect ($1.000$ of the rescued cell against a receiver at $0.000$), while
transplanting an equally long span of the question reproduces nothing beyond the
receiver's own baseline, and the final prompt position reproduces nothing at
all. How much of the decision a small position group can carry is in turn set by
how many tokens the answer occupies---$1.000$, $0.304$ and $0.000$ for a
one-token, a three-token and a chain-of-thought answer on the same items and
model. Eq.~\ref{eq:decomp} is therefore a decomposition of the state that
carries a decision. That is the state every activation-patching result about
in-context documents is about, and its content component turns out to be small,
inert-when-removed, and an almost perfect identifier of which document produced
it.

\paragraph{Contributions.}
\begin{enumerate}
\item \textbf{A subtraction protocol with a matched negative control}
(\S\ref{sec:decomp}), on a synthetic control whose floor is exactly zero and on
55 skills and 1{,}100 instances written by other people.
\item \textbf{Presence dominates geometry; content dominates behaviour.} The
presence component is the larger of the two over most of the network and repairs
$0.062$ of the rescued cell at every one of 28 layers---exactly what putting the
wrong document in the prompt achieves---while the content component repairs
$0.812$. Conclusions about content drawn from displacement norms or
cross-condition cosines are therefore unsafe.
\item \textbf{Which control you subtract chooses what you measure}
(\S\ref{sec:controls}). Against an unrelated document the content component
repairs $0.81$; against the same document with every number replaced, $0.31$.
\item \textbf{Injection capacity is set by answer length}
(\S\ref{sec:onepos}). On one model and one item set, the final-position patch
that reproduces $1.000$ of the rescued cell in multiple choice reproduces
$0.304$ in free-form; on third-party skills answered through a chain of thought,
neither the final position nor a 128-position span transplant reproduces
anything the \emph{wrong} skill's span does not also reproduce. The range over
which ``a skill's effect is carried by a vector'' is the range over which the
answer is short.
\item \textbf{A layer-resolved account of where the content is readable}
(\S\ref{sec:where}), and knockouts showing that no single pathway is necessary
and that the model stops reading the document at a specific layer.
\item \textbf{What the content component is a property of} (\S\ref{sec:whose}):
its direction identifies the skill, its effect does not transfer at all.
\item \textbf{Two measurement traps} (\S\ref{sec:traps}), each with a
quantitative decomposition: an aggregate log-probability that ranks a
content-free control \emph{above} the true state, and a multiple-choice framing
under which a document with every number wrong retains two thirds of the effect.
\end{enumerate}

\section{Setup}
\label{sec:setup}

\subsection{Two task families}

\paragraph{Real skills (main).} MedCalc-Bench instances with the 55 gold
calculator skills released with SRA-Bench: $55$ calculators $\times$ $20$
instances $=1{,}100$ items, graded deterministically against a numeric
tolerance with no model in the loop. Both the skills and the tasks are other
people's, which is what makes the effect size credible. Model: Qwen3-8B, single
turn, no tools, greedy. Confidence intervals are bootstrapped over
\emph{calculators}, not instances, because the 20 items sharing a calculator are
not independent.

\paragraph{Synthetic positive control.} A fictional unit system (three families
of units, an invented conversion table) with a one-page skill document giving
the table. Because the units are invented, the no-document floor is guaranteed
and contamination is impossible; because the document is ours, we know exactly
what content means. The item set is generated from the table
($n=358$); every item whose answer also appears in a worked example of the
document is dropped, so no item can be solved by copying.

\subsection{Two dependent variables, and why both}

We report (i) \textbf{accuracy}, from a greedily decoded free-form answer graded
by the task's own scorer, and (ii) the \textbf{teacher-forced log-probability}
of the gold answer. They fail differently and disagree often enough that
reporting one alone is not safe (\S\ref{sec:traps}); accuracy is read first
throughout. Notably, none of our items was rewritten into multiple choice to
obtain an accuracy channel---\S\ref{sec:format} shows why that rewrite is not
harmless.

\subsection{Four cells}
\label{sec:cells}

Every item is labelled by what the document did to it:
\textbf{R} (rescued: wrong without, right with),
\textbf{F} (persistent: wrong both ways),
\textbf{K} (kept: right both ways),
\textbf{B} (broken: right without, wrong with).
\textbf{R is the only cell in which the document demonstrably works}, and every
table in this paper is read by cell. \S\ref{sec:traps} shows that the
aggregate---over all four---can be not merely noisy but sign-inverted relative
to R.

